An old book, my dear interlocutor, is a tactile sonnet to the past. The pages, thin and brittle as the wings of a moth, whisper tales of yesteryears under the gentle caress of your fingers. The cover, worn and weathered, bears the battle scars of time, while the spine, creased and cracked, is like the weary backbone of history itself.
