To create a store management application that offers real-time profit tracking and analysis for the store owner, you can use Python libraries such as Django, Flask, or PyQt5 to build the frontend and backend of the application. These libraries are versatile and provide a robust framework for developing applications. Here's a sample Python code that demonstrates how to integrate the total profit formula into the application, ensuring that the calculation is seamlessly included in the store management system:

