In this code, we define a function `reverse_odd_words` that takes a sentence as input. The sentence is split into individual words using the `split()` method. We then iterate through each word and check if it has an odd number of letters. If so, we reverse the word using slicing with a step of -1 (`[::-1]`). Finally, we join the modified words back into a sentence using the `join()` method and return the reversed sentence.
