print(reverse_list([1, 2, 3, 4, 5]))  # Output: [5, 4, 3, 2, 1]
print(reverse_list([1, -2, 3, 4, -5]))  # Output: [-5, 4, 3, -2, 1]
```

The function returns the expected outputs for the sample inputs, and it has a time complexity of O(n) and a space complexity of O(1).
